{"book":20,"chapter":9,"context":{"chapter":9,"title":"Two Banquets, Two Hostesses","summary":"Lady Wisdom prepares a feast and invites the simple to live, while Folly calls out the same invitation to guests who end up among the dead. Between the two scenes stand sayings about scorners and the wise.","background":"Both women call from the city's high places (vv. 3, 14) and use the same opening line (vv. 4, 16), so the choice is between two equally public invitations. Wisdom serves meat and mixed wine, a lavish banquet. The meaning of her 'seven pillars' (v. 1) is debated; at least it pictures a large, finished house.","customs":[{"term":"Stolen waters","verses":"9:17","note":"Water pictured sexual pleasure in 5:15-18. Folly's 'stolen waters' recall that warning: secrecy is her whole appeal."}],"watchFor":["Verse 10 echoes 1:7, framing chapters 1–9 with the fear of the Lord.","Folly offers bread and water; Wisdom offers bread, meat and wine."],"connections":["Psalms 111:10","Isaiah 55:1-2","Matthew 22:2-4","Luke 14:16-17"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["חָכְמוֹת","chakhemot","H2451","HNcfpa","wisdom<s>"],["בָּנְתָה","banetah","H1129","HVqp3fs","she has built"],["בֵיתָהּ","veitah","H1004","HNcmsc/Sp3fs","house her"],["חָצְבָה","chatzevah","H2672","HVqp3fs","she has hewn"],["עַמּוּדֶיהָ","'amudeiha","H5982","HNcmpc/Sp3fs","pillars her"],["שִׁבְעָה","shiv'ah","H7651","HAcbsa","seven"]],"x":[[40016018,40016018,7],[66003012,66003012,6],[11007002,11007003,5],[46003009,46003015,5],[48002009,48002009,5],[49002020,49002022,5],[60002005,60002006,5],[11007021,11007021,4],[58003003,58003006,4],[11007006,11007006,3]],"xn":11},"2":{"w":[["טָבְחָה","tavechah","H2873","HVqp3fs","she has slaughtered"],["טִבְחָהּ","tivchah","H2874","HNcmsc/Sp3fs","slaughtering her"],["מָסְכָה","masekhah","H4537","HVqp3fs","she has mixed"],["יֵינָהּ","yeinah","H3196","HNcmsc/Sp3fs","wine her"],["אַף","'af","H637","HTj","also"],["עָרְכָה","'arekhah","H6186","HVqp3fs","she has arranged"],["שֻׁלְחָנָהּ","shulchan